where we applied (1, eq. (2.21)) for the evaluation of the inner product between conformal blocks. It reads

$$ \langle\mathcal{F}_{g,n}^{\mathcal{C}}(\vec{P})\,|\,\mathcal{F}_{g,n}^{\mathcal{C}}(\vec{P}^{\prime})\rangle=\frac{\delta^{3g-3+n}(\vec{P}-\vec{P}^{\prime})}{\prod_{\text{cuffs a}}\rho_{0}(P_{a})\prod_{\text{pair of pants }(i,j,k)}C_{0}(P_{i},P_{j},P_{k})}\ . $$

Here, $\mathcal{F}^{\mathcal{C}}_{g,n}$ are the genus- $g$ $n$ -point Virasoro blocks in a particular OPE channel $\mathcal{C}$ , $C_{0}(P_{1},P_{2},P_{3})$ is the Liouville three-point function, and $\rho_{0}(P)$ the inverse of the two-point function. In other words, conformal blocks in a channel $\mathcal{C}$ are orthogonal with a density given by the inverse OPE density of Liouville theory. See [1] for our conventions for the Liouville structure constants.

