This contributes to a different sixth moment of the structure constants

$$ |Z_{\text{Vir}}(M)|^{2}\leftrightarrow\overline{c_{1a2}c_{2b3}c_{3c4}c_{4a5}c_{5b6}c_{6c1}}. $$

We could of course compute the TQFT partition function on this wormhole by a straightforward Heegaard splitting, for example along three four-punctured spheres. In this case it turns out to be most convenient to replace the three-punctured sphere boundaries with trivalent junctions as in (27) and hence regard the wormhole as a network of Wilson lines embedded in $\mathrm{S}^{3}$ :

$$ \displaystyle Z_{\text{Vir}}(M) \displaystyle=\mathsf{C}_{12a}\mathsf{C}_{23b}\mathsf{C}_{34c}\mathsf{C}_{45a}\mathsf{C}_{56b}\mathsf{C}_{61c}\,Z_{\text{Vir}}\Bigg(\vbox{\hbox{
