## Appendix A Semiclassical expansion of the double sine function

In this appendix, we will derive the semiclassical expansion of the double sine function (135). We start from the integral representation

$$ \displaystyle\log S_{b}(x_{0}+x) \displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{\mathbb{R}+i0^{+}}\frac{\text{d}t}{t}\,\frac{\sinh\big((\frac{Q}{2}-x-x_{0})t\big)}{\sinh(\frac{bt}{2})\sinh(\frac{t}{2b})} \displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{\mathbb{R}+i0^{+}}\frac{\text{d}t}{t}\,\frac{\mathrm{e}^{(\frac{b^{2}+1}{2}-bx-bx_{0})t}-\mathrm{e}^{-(\frac{b^{2}+1}{2}-bx-bx_{0})t}}{(\mathrm{e}^{\frac{b^{2}t}{2}}-\mathrm{e}^{-\frac{b^{2}t}{2}})\sinh(\frac{t}{2})} \displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{(\mathbb{R}+i0^{+})\cup(\mathbb{R}+i0^{-})}\frac{\text{d}t}{t}\,\frac{\mathrm{e}^{(b^{2}+\frac{1}{2}-bx-bx_{0})t}}{(\mathrm{e}^{b^{2}t}-1)\sinh(\frac{t}{2})}\ . $$

Here we rescaled $t$ and put $t\to-t$ in the second expression to have the integrand have the same form. We can now use the definition of the Bernoulli polynomials and get as formal expansion

$$ \displaystyle\log S_{b}(x_{0}+x) \displaystyle=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{b^{2n-2}}{4n!}\,B_{n}(1-\tfrac{x}{b})\int_{(\mathbb{R}+i0^{+})\cup(\mathbb{R}+i0^{-})}\text{d}t\,\frac{t^{n-2}\,\mathrm{e}^{(\frac{1}{2}-bx_{0})t}}{\sinh(\frac{t}{2})}\ . $$

The remaining integral can be computed for example by pulling off the contour off and summing over the residues at $t=2\pi im$ . This gives

$$ \displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}+i0^{+}}\text{d}t\,\frac{t^{n-2}\,\mathrm{e}^{(\frac{1}{2}-bx_{0})t}}{\sinh(\frac{t}{2})} \displaystyle=\sum_{m=1}^{\infty}2(2\pi im)^{n-2}\,\mathrm{e}^{-2\pi imbx_{0}}=2(2\pi i)^{n-2}\text{Li}_{2-n}(\mathrm{e}^{-2\pi ibx_{0}})\ . $$

We similarly evaluate the contribution from the other contour $\mathbb{R}+i0^{-}$ which then recovers (135).

